## What your wares fetch
What your wares fetch in coin — use it to set a fair price or weigh a trade:
- Flour: your own produce — it sells in bulk to Josiah Thorne, whose shop stocks it for the village, not to folk directly. Folk pay about 4 coins each in the shops, it costs you about 1 coin each to produce, but the shop has lately paid you about 3 coins each. Send other buyers to Josiah Thorne.
- Wheat: 1 to 2 coins each; you have lately paid about 1 coin each for it — ask 2 coins or more at your counter; your shop lives on the difference. Keep 10 back for making your own Flour; only the 37 beyond that are yours to sell.

A buyer's offer awaits your answer — settle it first with accept_pay, decline_pay, or counter_pay, before tending to your own needs.
